# `std`'s own root file -- unlike `core` (see `runtime/core/core.omg`),
# `std` gets no ambient-prelude/eager-discovery privilege of its own: it's
# an ordinary `--extern` package, the same way `plat` is (see
# `docs/22-platform-glue.md`), consumed via explicit `import std::list::List;`
# and friends. This file still has nothing to declare -- it exists only
# because it is the root module when `std` is compiled standalone.
